  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, acc=0.639) establishes that multimodal + multiprofile + avgpool + weighted is the strongest combination. The image encoder choice (resnet50 vs vit_l) shows negligible difference (~0.4%), and avgpool clearly outperforms transformer aggregation. However, the RNA encoder has only been tested as pca_n2000 (a linear projection). The most important remaining uncertainty is whether a learned RNA representation (scvi_n200) can capture richer biological structure and improve over PCA. This experiment (config_031) tests scvi_n200 while holding all other parameters at their best-known values (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted), isolating the effect of the RNA encoder. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information experiment: if scvi improves, it opens a promising direction; if not, it confirms PCA is sufficient and we can focus remaining budget on other axes."
}

